  "notes": "n = 10 x 7, coprime. The even factor is the board entry n10-3e6da6ff4ea68349b07d, with one row negated where needed so that every position has product 1; the odd factor is n7-ad2db6a1c641e13aaa4e. Each quadruple is read position by position as a quaternion through the correspondence tabulated in the cited paper, the two sequences are multiplied entrywise with indices taken modulo their lengths, and the product is read back as four rows."
